  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">New Digital Financial Inclusion</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Productividad del Sector Privado</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(El Salvador):  The Digital Financial Inclusion activity will support small and medium enterprises (SMEs), especially those led by women and community members at risk of irregular migration, to grow and increase incomes. It will also support remittance recipients to improve their access to financial products and services. The activity will help businesses adopt new technologies to better meet the credit and savings needs of growth-oriented SMEs. The activity will design, pilot, and roll-out the delivery of digital and financial education content, and promote the adoption of digital wallets and other digital means of payment. Through financial education and customized financial services and products, the activity will enable remittance recipients to obtain more value per dollar received. It will increase linkages to digital wallets to save, borrow, and make payments more efficiently and safely. The activity will advance gender equality by incorporating digital campaigns and behavior change communications that increase women&apos;s use of digital financial services and control over resources. The majority of El Salvador&apos;s economy is driven by informal, financially excluded, and offline business, with persistent gender disparities. The Digital Financial Inclusion activity will partner with Mastercard and financial services providers to increase access and use of formal and digital finance to help unleash growth of Salvadoran businesses, particularly female-owned, and unlock the potential of remittance recipients to maximize the use of the funds they receive. Through private sector partnerships, the activity supports ICS MO 3.1 and RCS Pillar I by supporting SMEs to enhance their hard and soft business skills, and by training SMEs on digital tools for business management, marketing, and sales.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Mejorar la capacidad de las empresas para integrarse a los mercados nacionales e internacionales mediante aumentos de la productividad y mejoras en el gobierno corporativo y el desarrollo y aplicaci&#xF3;n de tecnolog&#xED;a y pr&#xE1;cticas de marketing modernas. Mejorar la capacidad de las empresas y asociaciones empresariales en t&#xE9;rminos de sus capacidades de gobierno corporativo y su aplicaci&#xF3;n de mejores pr&#xE1;cticas y tecnolog&#xED;as para lograr una mayor producci&#xF3;n y comercializaci&#xF3;n de productos y servicios. Incluye la adopci&#xF3;n de procesos de producci&#xF3;n eficientes, una mayor productividad laboral, una gesti&#xF3;n ambientalmente racional de los recursos naturales y el desarrollo de sistemas de contabilidad y gesti&#xF3;n que puedan ayudar a la empresa y al grupo industrial a implementar est&#xE1;ndares comerciales, laborales, de productos y de procesos que mejoren la competitividad empresarial. Los programas de desarrollo de capacidad empresarial pueden incluir actividades que ayuden a las empresas y asociaciones propiedad de hombres y mujeres a responder a estos mercados internacionales y crear alianzas regionales.</narrative>
  </description>
